  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nThe Four Corners ridge will remain with continued flattening \nover the region from upper-level troughing remaining offshore. \nTemperatures will be near normal to 5 degrees above normal \nthrough the period. Monsoon moisture will continue to reach far \nSE Oregon and southwest ID south of the Snake Basin through \nearly next week. There is increasing confidence in a slight \nchance of thunderstorms along the NV border each afternoon.\nWesterly flow aloft will continue breezy conditions, especially\nduring the afternoons and early evenings. Smoky conditions will\ncontinue from area wildfires which may keep temperatures \nslightly cooler than forecast. By Thursday, a significant\npattern change is being converged upon by long range models. The\nupper-level troughing that has been sitting offshore until now\nmoves inland, bringing cooler temperatures and better chances of\nprecipitation than the area has seen in some time. As with most\nthings this far in the long term, these details are fickle and\nsubject to quick changes forecast to forecast.",
